@flexiarg operator/continue-against-a-named-curriculum
@title Continue Against A Named Curriculum
@status accepted 2026-11-11: proposed by 象 for 9 turns (Joe 2026-11-11: recurrence suffices); attested once used in a mission or a War Machine cascade
@provenance 象 proposals, ~/.emacs-graph/session-turn-analysis/<record>[.json].candidates.json; records: turn-B4uQ4S turn-GxkKom turn-KrdAAA turn-Sh1Sfq turn-YnE8TC turn-heMCxh turn-hvAlC5 turn-oCTsYq turn-t4Q4wl
@parent devmap-coherence/next-steps-to-done
@context The operator resumes an already-running delegated implementation task and the agent could otherwise treat 'keep going' as open-ended effort.

! conclusion: Bind the continuation to a named external curriculum or milestone list, defining progress as discrete steps towards it.

  + IF:
    Work is mid-flight and the operator says to continue it.

  + HOWEVER:
    A bare 'continue' leaves the agent free to count any activity as progress; without an external yardstick, continuation can drift.

  + THEN:
    Bind the continuation to a named external curriculum or milestone list, defining progress as discrete steps towards it.

  + BECAUSE:
    Next-steps-to-done tracks explicit steps toward completion inside a devmap; this move applies the same discipline at delegation time by pointing at an external curriculum as the done-list.
